			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Hydrate URI results and use Mountain for glob-based extension activation\n\nTwo related improvements to the workspace namespace and extension activation flow:\n\n1. URI Result Hydration: Add HydrateUriResults helper that converts string URLs returned from Mountain's findFiles effect into proper vscode.Uri objects. Extensions expect result[i].fsPath / .scheme / .toString() to work, but Mountain returns raw strings. Uses Stock VS Code's URI.parse() to create fully-functional URI instances.\n\n2. Mountain-Backed Glob Activation: Add FolderContainsGlobViaMountain that calls findFiles(glob, {maxResults:1}) via gRPC. The activation logic now:\n   - Uses native stat for literal filenames (package.json, Cargo.toml)\n   - Uses Mountain's parallel ignore::WalkBuilder for glob patterns\n   - Falls back to local Node walker on Mountain miss/IPC failure\n\n3. Output: Remove Configuration directory (ESBuild, Plugin, Polyfill, Service configs and tsconfig files) from the Output element.\n\nImpact: Extensions now receive proper Uri objects with full fsPath/scheme/toString() support. Glob-based activation leverages Mountain's OS-threaded, gitignore-aware walker with early-exit for faster activation on large repos.",
			"SHA": "6a4ea12074ce46f5dd1efe0d69dd48e9e067f57a"
		},
